acy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kleonc/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This should probably mention that [it plays the first/last frame once aka it's frame based ping pong, not time based](https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/11698#issuecomment-4054400181). But this is a documentation for SpriteFrames, and SpriteFrames itself doesn't handle how the loop mode is processed/interpreted, this is done by AnimationSprite2D/3D. So it should probably say that specifically AnimationSprite2D/3D plays it that way? 🤔\n```suggestion\n\t\t\tThe animation alternates direction each time it reaches the end or start, playing forward and then in reverse repeatedly.\n\t\t\t[b]Note:[/b] Both [AnimationSprite2D] and [AnimationSprite3D] play the first/last frame for its duration only once at each end of the animation (instead of twice i.e. once per forward/backward animation direction).\n```","created_at":"2026-03-19T12:09:43Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T12:10:51Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114556#discussion_r2959628216","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114556","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2959628216"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114556#discussion_r2959628216"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114556"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2959628216/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":null,"original_start_line":null,"start_side":null,"line":178,"original_line":178,"side":"RIGHT","author_association":"MEMBER","original_position":57,"position":57,"subject_type":"line"},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2961718890","pull_request_review_id":