/jgill88","html_url":"https://github.com/jgill88","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/jgill88/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks for the review! Yeah that is definitely more concise. \r\n\r\nI wasn't sure how 'defensive' to be in here.. in theory, `d[\"loop\"]` could be anything, but most likely it's loading a value that the engine wrote. It looks like other areas of the engine use `static_cast<::LoopMode>`, so happy to follow suit there. And I did verify that the bool variant correctly casts to LOOP_NONE/LOOP_LINEAR. Updated.\r\n\r\n> Regarding the looping methods at both ends, it might be worth documenting that when a loop like 11234566 is needed, you can use frame_progress as I mentioned in https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7643#issuecomment-4057898440. From that https://github.com/godotengine/godot-proposals/issues/7643#issuecomment-4057898440, ideally, we should probably allow 0 in frame time scale, but since that could make special cases too complex, I think we can follow up on that in a separate PR if it's really necessary.\r\n\r\nI was struggling a little bit with how to concisely document this. Disclaimer that I went back and forth with ChatGPT (meh), the best I came up with was:\r\n\r\n> Note: To accomplish time-based ping pong, double the duration of the first and last frame. When starting an animation, set the [AnimatedSprite2D] or [AnimatedSprite3D] [code]frame_progress[/code] member to `0.5` in order to avoid doubling the first frame's playback time.","created_at":"2026-03-24T05:41:41Z","updated_at":"2026-03-24T05:41:41Z","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114556#discussion_r2979134066","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114556","_links":{"self":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2979134066"},"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/114556#discussion_r2979134066"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/114556"}},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/comments/2979134066/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"start_line":219,"original_start_line":219,"start_side":"RIGHT","line":221,"original_line":226,"side":"RIGHT","in_reply_to_id":2963096309,"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","original_position":42,"position":37,"subject_type":"line"}]